As we all know, Maggie is...

251
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:14,820
Channel 19 News.

252
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:21,680
And behind the camera, she's a busy mother of four.

253
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:27,320
Maggie, come on up here and tell us how you do it all.

254
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:30,880
Whoo! Whoo! Whoo -hoo!

255
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:33,660
Who the heck are you?

256
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:34,940
I'm accepting for Maggie.

257
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:35,600
She didn't do it.

258
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:36,720
She's working. Oh.

259
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:42,580
Oh. Hello, fellow working mothers.

260
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:47,180
Hey, buddy, who the heck are you?

261
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:50,140
I'm Maggie's husband, Jason.

262
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:51,660
She couldn't be here tonight.

263
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:55,020
Oh. Thank you.

264
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:59,920
But she did ask me to share with you some of her thoughts.

265
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:01,200
So here goes.

266
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:03,740
A funny thing happened to her on the way to the banquet tonight.

267
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:08,180
She knew she forgot something, and then she remembered her opening joke.

268
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:10,340
Ha ha ha ha ha.

269
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:12,120
Ha ha ha ha ha!

270
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:17,480
Oh, that man told us to laugh.

271
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:19,600
Ha ha ha ha ha!

272
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:26,060
So, uh, I don't think I could possibly do, uh, justice to my wife's wonderful

273
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:31,120
speech, so I think I'll just share with you my impression of my wife.

274
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:34,280
This is as bad as the Sylvester Stallone impression.

275
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:35,700
and these babes are gonna tear him apart.

276
00:16:36,060 --> 00:16:40,460
Why, shoot, but I think it's best summed up in one moment from last night.

277
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:44,120
I had been away on a trip and it was very late.

278
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:47,640
Mm -hmm. Oh, hi, honey.

279
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:50,060
Oh, boy, am I glad to see you.

280
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:54,000
Being at a convention with 200 psychiatrists for three days straight is enough to

281
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,500
drive a person totally insane.

282
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:58,680
I heard enough knock -knock jokes to last a lifetime.

283
00:16:59,260 --> 00:17:02,900
I know you promised to wait up for me, sweetheart, and I have to admit, I didn't

284
00:17:02,900 --> 00:17:03,520
think you would.

285
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:09,180
You know, it's kind of late, but I sure appreciate that you did and I love you.

286
00:17:11,680 --> 00:17:13,480
I wanted to talk to you.

287
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:18,740
Are you sleeping, sweetheart?

288
00:17:21,320 --> 00:17:24,500
Sweetheart. The baby.

289
00:17:25,620 --> 00:17:28,200
Oh, honey, as long as you're up, will you check on Chrissy?

290
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:30,620
There's plenty of diapers in the car.

291
00:17:32,440 --> 00:17:34,800
Yeah, of course I will, my dear.

292
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:37,020
No problem. Nice talking to you.

293
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,660
Jason, sweetheart, welcome home.

294
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:47,400
I missed you, love.

295
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:49,240
Guess who? P.S.

296
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:52,320
Hope it wasn't another marathon of knock -knock jokes.

297
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:54,260
P.P.S.

298
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:58,280
Ramon, darling, if you're reading this, please put it back.

299
00:17:58,380 --> 00:17:59,880
It's for my husband, Jason.

300
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:07,800
It's midnight and in local headlines, those secret garbage strike talks broke off

301
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:12,340
late tonight when garbage czar, Red Cohen, punched out labor leader, Happy

302
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:15,920
Spreckles, who says he's considering changing his nickname.

303
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:22,880
It's over. The dinner's over.

304
00:18:23,240 --> 00:18:25,040
Uh -huh. Oh, no.

305
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:28,600
I'm sure in a dress like that, you'll have no problem finding a meal.

306
00:18:29,220 --> 00:18:30,600
Oh, no. I'm sorry.

307
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:34,500
No, see, I was supposed to accept the Working Mother of the Year Award tonight.

308
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:37,320
Oh, is this an international competition?

309
00:18:37,940 --> 00:18:40,860
No, it's the Long Island Professional Women's Association.

310
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,740
Oh, then I had no shot.

311
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:44,020
I live in the Bronx.

312
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:48,380
Does sound kind of silly, doesn't it?

313
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:51,160
No, but I'm glad I didn't win the award.

314
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:52,980
Just another thing to dust.

315
00:18:55,320 --> 00:19:00,060
Oh. Oh, go ahead.

316
00:19:00,260 --> 00:19:01,400
I won't tell a soul.

317
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:12,700
You wouldn't happen to want a pickle, would you?

318
00:19:13,260 --> 00:19:15,540
Yeah. I can take my break a little earlier.

319
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:19,100
Hot pastrami would go great with this.

320
00:19:20,020 --> 00:19:20,980
You're out of luck.

321
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:27,120
Oh. Say, you look familiar to me.

322
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:29,680
I'm a reporter for the Channel 19 News.

323
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:31,620
My Ishtar station?

324
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:36,500
That's us. I'm Maggie.

325
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:40,660
Kathleen. I'm a cleaning woman.

326
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:42,640
I sense that.

327
00:19:44,420 --> 00:19:45,720
How's the cheesecake?

328
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:48,960
Ah, it's a bit warmer than I like it.

329
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:49,940
Same with the pickle.

330
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:58,260
You know, I'll bet you are the working mother of the year.

331
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:00,060
How could you tell?

332
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:02,620
You didn't have time to pick up the award.

333
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:08,120
You know, Kathleen, I...

334
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:10,560
I didn't really care about getting the award.

335
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:15,660
Exactly. And I know it doesn't mean much.

336
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:18,180
It's just that it's...

337
00:20:18,180 --> 00:20:20,820
Well, it's nice to be recognized every now and then.

338
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:26,140
Yeah, I was the employee of the month in this hotel in June.

339
00:20:26,580 --> 00:20:32,380
Really? 1957. That's nice.

340
00:20:32,820 --> 00:20:34,720
Oh, you know what's nice?

341
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:40,620
That day, all four of my kids and my husband took me out to dinner.

342
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:45,480
And they wouldn't let me lift a finger in the apartment the entire weekend.

343
00:20:45,980 --> 00:20:47,660
Now that was nice.

344
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:02,460
Well, I should be getting home to my four kids and my husband.

345
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:08,460
It's been nice talking to you, Kathleen.

346
00:21:08,620 --> 00:21:09,840
Oh, same here.

347
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:14,900
Hold on. You forgot your award.

348
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:23,880
What? Here. Thanks.

349
00:21:25,300 --> 00:21:29,100
Speech. Speech. Okay.

350
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:32,860
Oh, never mind.

351
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:49,400
Working mother of the year.

352
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:57,740
I'm sorry. Welcome home to my favorite working mother of the year.

353
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:01,580
We all missed you tonight, but no one more than me.

354
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:03,200
Love, guess who?

355
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:07,280
P.S. They loved your speech, even though I know I didn't do it justice.

356
00:22:07,820 --> 00:22:08,720
P.P.S.

357
00:22:09,060 --> 00:22:11,260
Ramon, you are one lucky hombre.

358
00:22:30,380 --> 00:22:50,940
I'm sorry. Oh, sure glad I won this.

359
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:00,720
A 28 -year -old man?

360
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:03,980
Oh, you talked to Mom, I see.

361
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:05,280
Carol, what were you thinking?

362
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,340
Well, possibly, Dad.

363
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:10,180
Mom did not convey the complete picture of what occurred yesterday.

364
00:23:10,180 --> 00:23:11,120
Was he 28?

365
00:23:11,540 --> 00:23:12,860
Yes. Was he bald?

366
00:23:13,660 --> 00:23:16,420
Technically. And was he taking you out?

367
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:17,220
In a way.

368
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:19,280
That's complete picture enough for me.

369
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:21,440
All right, Dad.

370
00:23:21,680 --> 00:23:22,740
Learned my lesson.

371
00:23:23,160 --> 00:23:27,240
From now on, my date age limit will be 27, tops.

372
00:23:27,580 --> 00:23:30,000
19. 24. 19.

373
00:23:30,380 --> 00:23:31,780
How about 19?

374
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:33,880
That's a good compromise.

375
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:38,920
As long as he also has a full head of bushy, healthy hair.

376
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:44,400
Fine. But, Carol, I love you.

